      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T19:27:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A few things to consider.\n- We pass sampler2Ds today; this seems like it won\u0027t work with today\u0027s Graphite. It we want to forbid this, the first step seems like it would be fixing Graphite. https://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/sksl/sksl_graphite_frag.sksl;l\u003d50;drc\u003dbd3fc2d942e5794c036c89507b4ffc2134f79573\n- We should reject things in the backend only as a last resort. This error check could happen in the frontend in `check_parameters` https://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/sksl/ir/SkSLFunctionDeclaration.cpp;l\u003d70;drc\u003d8ca279c255bcaef58b37f328a9029abbfa818312\n- This doesn\u0027t seem like an appropriate use of assertions, unless we think that we\u0027ve forbidden them in the frontend and that it\u0027s impossible to reach this point. We should report user-code errors using the ErrorReporter.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1181,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1187,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ee6328615d7b6f5a0e25c9d6a968e1a702736641",
