      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T20:12:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All of your comments make sense and I\u0027ll work on them soon.\n\nRe your first point around currently passing sampler2Ds in sksl_graphite_frag.sksl: this has been a point of friction for the Graphite+Dawn work during the sprint and I have summarized where we are with the prototyping so far at https://bugs.chromium.org/p/skia/issues/detail?id\u003d13806#c26. PTAL!\n\njamesgk@ and I discussed this quite a bit during the sprint and I have a working prototype that separates the unified sampler parameters in an exploration branch, see https://chromium.googlesource.com/experimental/external/gob/skia/skia/+/329acf77fb5f9f159385723fe221b095929420d7 and https://chromium.googlesource.com/experimental/external/gob/skia/skia/+/43ee9c601dda30f822c785a11c1908f3f9bb020d.\n\nMy current thinking was to land this CL first without effecting functionality in Metal (the Vulkan/Dawn backends aren\u0027t far enough along in Skia\u0027s mainline to be affected). I can alternately turn the experimental changes above into proper CLs first, test them on Metal, and then move on to the SPIR-V changes if you think that order makes more sense. (That would actually make it easier to address your other comments around catching these in the front-end graphite will have moved off the pattern).\n\nI realize that skbug.com/13806 has gotten fairly large and I intend to file independent bugs for all of these subtasks and document them thoroughly.",
      "parentUuid": "79ad1ad2_4cf3a729",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1181,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1187,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ee6328615d7b6f5a0e25c9d6a968e1a702736641",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a92dbf79_31a31e84",
        "filename": "src/sksl/codegen/SkSLSPIRVCodeGenerator.cpp",
