      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T20:31:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we land this CL, it\u0027s free money for the fuzzer; it can easily generate a shader which hits this assertion. \n\nLet\u0027s assume that we change this error to use the ErrorReporter to dodge that issue. Then, landing this change in mainline would put us in a state where we can\u0027t pass split sampler/textures (unsupported in Metal), and we can\u0027t pass unified sampler/textures (unsupported in Dawn). That seems like a bad place to be in.\n\nUnfortunately fixing Metal to work properly with separate-samplers is going to take some doing; I don\u0027t see any support for `kSeparateSampler` in Metal today. (Metal has all the moving parts; we just need to implement it.)\n\nIf you guys have a separate branch for the exploration sprint, would it be better to land this there? I don\u0027t see any rush to land this in mainline today, and while it solves a problem for Dawn, AFAICS it adds a problem for Greg in the short term as he works on Vulkan support for Graphite.",
      "parentUuid": "d958d3ca_bca5d589",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1181,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1187,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ee6328615d7b6f5a0e25c9d6a968e1a702736641",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97b1e523_fd2ad0a4",
